{
  "comment": "The markdown of an answer read into blocks (D-303). This is the part of markdown Claude writes; everything else stays text. A line break inside a paragraph is kept. Code is only fenced, and a fence that was not closed runs to the end, so a text that is still being written reads the same way. Inside a paragraph a numbered list begins only at one. An inline is text, code, strong, emphasis, strike or a link; a picture is a link, because Aiko loads nothing from the internet.",
